      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "that world is using a script to shuffle things around when you're flying around in a plane. i'm including a little video that shows where my avatar thinks it is in the world, note how the z gets up to 2777 and then the coordinates all change. the \"world movement script\" is moving everything to keep the player within 5000-6000 meters of the origin point. if you go to that world and use the avatar flight, you can fly out until you have the floating point issue.\n\nhttps://vrchat.com/home/world/wrld_7a001430-07b4-42f8-b24e-206a8dc75a8e/info this is just how i prefer worlds to be linked, so this is just for my benefit.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
